 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the village law, in relation to certain elections for fire\ncompanies in Croton-on-Hudson",
    "basePrintNo": "S7201",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7201-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§10-1010 & 10-1012, Vil L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7201\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the village law, in relation to certain elections for\nfire companies in Croton-on-Hudson\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo amend village law to address election procedures for fire companies\nin the village of Croton-on-Hudson.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 10-1010 of the village law to change the annual\nmeeting date for fire companies in the village of Croton-on-Hudson from\nthe first Tuesday in April to the first Tuesday in December. It also\nupdates the language regarding election procedures for company officers,\nwardens, and delegates, clarifying term lengths & disqualifications\nrelated to arson convictions.\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision one of section 10-1012 of the village to\nadjust the meeting date for elected delegates of the Croton-on-Hudson\nfire department to the Thursday following the first Tuesday in December.\nIt also updates provisions regarding the nomination and appointment\nprocess for fire department officers.\n\nSection 3 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Village of Croton-on-Hudson's fire department previously adjusted\nits election schedule to align terms of office with the Length of\nService Award Program (LOSAP) pension, which operates on a calendar-year\nbasis. This alignment ensures consistency in leadership transitions and\nsimplifies administrative processes related to service awards. With\nLOSAP having successfully completed its initial 20-year period, Village\nresidents demonstrated strong support for its continuation, voting over-\nwhelmingly (82%) in favor of extending the program for another 20 years\nin 2023.\n\nThis legislation comes at the request of the Village.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
